            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jessica Paige"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Holy moly this was good! Needed to find a way to use the fresh figs I had picked at my best friend's house. The combination was wonderful. I didn't use the food processor to grind up the figs and pine nuts, just cause I didn't have one available to me...but I think that it gave it a great textural element. Next time I might toast the nuts prior to combining them with the figs. Thank you Laura for sharing this recipe; this was a great way to end our Italian feast."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "lutzflcat"
            },
            "reviewBody": "9.1.18 My figs were very ripe, and I was concerned that if I put them in the blender, they’d turn to mush, so I chopped them as well as the pine nuts. Honestly, I did use the ingredients in the recipe, but I didn’t measure, just eyeballed everything. Definitely would roast the pine nuts in the future, but the nut-fig filling on the nectarines (yes, I used nectarines, not peaches) was very good. Super simple to make with nice presentation, actually a little elegant in its simplicity.",
            "datePublished": "2018-09-01T21:03:51.617Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ReikiCrone"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Really flavorful, but we topped it with a scoop of vanilla ice cream (husband) and/or a spoonful of greek yogurt (me). Perfect. Next time I dont think I will process the pine nuts and figs in the food processor, though. Needs a little contrasting texture and crunch.",
            "datePublished": "2011-09-01T14:10:05.877Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "mrs kosmos"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used nectarines instead of peaches. I liked the baked nectarines in the alcohol, but not the topping. If I make it again, I will reduce the amount of nuts and add a little honey to the topping. Also, based on DILLORDONEZ's review, I cut the alcohol in half, and it was still too much, so I'd cut it down even more.",
            "datePublished": "2010-08-19T19:56:14.503Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "DILLORDONEZ"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Absolutely delicious. Next time, though, I'll cut the alcohol by a lot. It was way more than needed and I felt like I was just wasting good wine.",
            "datePublished": "2010-07-30T20:08:24.317Z"
          }
